<title>USA: Union Carbide South Korean venture starts up plant.</title>
<headline>Union Carbide South Korean venture starts up plant.</headline>
<dateline>DANBURY, Conn. 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Carbide Corp said a 150,000 metric tonnes-per-year vinyl acetate monomer production unit in Ulsan, South Korea, has been started up.</p>
<p>The new plant is owned by a joint venture -- Asian Acetyls Co Ltd -- of Union Carbide, British Petroleum Co Plc's BP Chemicals and Samsung Group's Samsung Fine Chemicals Co.</p>
<p>The new facility is operated by SS-BP Chemicals Co Ltd, who are supplying it with acetic acid, the principal raw material, from their adjacent acid production unit.</p>
<p>Union Carbide said it will sell the vinyl acetate from Asian Acetyls outside of South Korea, and SS-BP Chemicals Co., Ltd. will sell within Korea.</p>
<p>Vinyl acetate monomer is used in the architectural coatings and adhesives industries and for production of emulsion resins for paper coatings and industrial products.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
